#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""b70: serve large MoE models on an Intel Arc Pro B70 (32 GB) with a RAM tier and an NVMe expert store.

    b70 setup [glm|flashnext|all]          one-time, CPU only: unpack the SGLang XPU image, fetch and build the kernels
    b70 info <model dir>                   JSON: which family the model is, whether setup and prepare are done
    b70 prepare <model dir> [--store DIR]  one-time per model: pack the NVMe expert store (GLM; Flash-Next fills its own)
    b70 serve <model dir> --port N [--ctx N] [--parallel N] [--name NAME] [--store DIR] [--all-ram]
                                           OpenAI-compatible server in the foreground; SIGTERM stops it
    b70 stop                               stop a running `b70 serve`
    b70 status                             JSON: the running server, if any

Families (by config.json model_type):
  glm        GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 (glm5_next): glm/ (exllamav3 fork + B70 tier), one request at a time
  flashnext  Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 (qwen4_exp): trellis-serve (SGLang 0.5.20-xpu + exl3xpu) with flashnext/'s patch

Everything runs inside the unpacked lmsysorg/sglang XPU image through bubblewrap; no Docker, no root. `serve` is also a
guard: it stops the server at the first xe fault on the B70, when RAM runs low, or when another GPU job opens the B70.

State lives in B70_STATE (default <repo>/state): the image, per-family overlays, the trellis-serve checkout, caches,
expert stores, logs. B70_ROOTFS points at an already unpacked image instead; B70_TRELLIS_SRC at a trellis-serve
checkout to use as is (development).
"""
